      ],
      "delivery_goal": "Deliver the complete protocol-neutral public harness.oac.dev/v1 SDK boundary with typed Describe, execute, observe, cancel, result, and error unions; preserve exact Package/entrypoint, Extension/binding, operation, owner, subject, scope, request digest, and service payload digest through every public binding path. Remove every public authority constructor that lets a caller choose both Host signing and trust verification inputs, and expose only the package-neutral consumer/verification side of opaque service and Gate handoffs. The SDK must define a usable Host-facing ingress contract without implementing the Host producer: arbitrary callers and ExtensionPackages must be unable to mint an authoritative RequestScope, GateEvaluatorBinding, receipt, or evaluator invocation. Replace the obsolete missing-symbol regression with a structurally valid attempt against the current public API and prove zero binding, receipt, and evaluator calls. Remove all SDK-owned or same-package test-only Host authority bridges. Every SDK-local fixture must emit source-revision-bound measured evidence for its exact scoped assertion; the Gate consumer row may pass only by proving the negative boundary, must report registered_gate_positive_path_count=0 and authoritative_gate_positive_claim_count=0, and must identify its scope as sdk-boundary rather than representing full Host-backed Gate conformance. Produce harness-sdk-boundary-evidence for the downstream harness-host producer. Preserve typed operation-schema validation, successful Trigger/EventHandler, bounded offline schema resolution, Required/Optional behavior, Unknown recovery, safe retry/cancel, coverage, race, vet, and deterministic sdk/harness packaging. The mandatory genuine Host-installed positive path and final combined semantic verdict remain downstream responsibilities of harness-host and contracts-extension. SDK-local positive operation conformance is not Host authorization: the fixed SDK conformance runner may execute ordinary typed Describe/Guide/Sensor/Executor/Trigger/EventHandler implementations with deterministic, non-authoritative request data and the same production input/response/schema/outcome validation and receipt-classification code. Its measured conformance records must be explicitly scoped sdk-operation-conformance, must not construct trusted RequestScope, service/Gate handoffs or authoritative receipts, and must never be usable by production authority entry points. A helper-only predicate or direct implementation call that bypasses the shared validation/measurement path is insufficient. Preserve successful Trigger output and all three successful EventHandler lifecycle operations; error-only implementations must fail these positive fixtures. Production typed Guide/Sensor/Trigger/EventHandler paths must finish response and output-schema validation before accepting a receipt; invalid results yield rejected/failed measured outcomes, while valid business-error envelopes retain a separate failed business outcome and never count as positive operation success. Optional side-effecting failures may become skipped only when the external failure outcome is known; structured Unknown and unstructured errors remain Unknown and require observation/recovery. SDK service/Gate rows are exclusively sdk-consumer-negative: reject even internally consistent caller handoffs without issuing a binding, authoritative receipt, or implementation/evaluator call. Envelope, rotation, replay, payload and identity assertions in these rows prove rejection of untrusted candidates, not authentication or durable replay enforcement. The Host-facing ingress contract must be package-neutral and implementable by the separately owned harness-host producer, not an unconditional rejecting stub or a caller-selectable verifier; document the exact release/entrypoint, binding, operation, owner, subject, scope, request/service-payload digest, component/run, policy and evaluator identity handoff. Host